# Enum Mapping

**Rule:** When mapping enums to specific values (like strings or integers), do not use constructor parameters. Instead, use a getter with an exhaustive `switch` statement to return the corresponding values.

### ✅ Good Example
```dart
enum NetworkErrorCode {
  timeout,
  badResponse,
  cancelled;

  String get errorCode {
    switch (this) {
      case NetworkErrorCode.timeout:
        return 'timeout';
      case NetworkErrorCode.badResponse:
        return 'bad_response';
      case NetworkErrorCode.cancelled:
        return 'cancelled';
    }
  }
}
```

### ❌ Bad Example
```dart
enum NetworkErrorCode {
  timeout('timeout'),
  badResponse('bad_response'),
  cancelled('cancelled');

  final String code;
  const NetworkErrorCode(this.code);

  String get errorCode => code;
}
```
